    "sourceDefects": {
      "originalDraftNotes": "Both documents are LaTeX (xdvipdfmx) exports with a usable text layer for words; formulas and superscripts are flattened there, so all mathematics was read from the page images. Nine top-level problems as in the catalogue; printed sub-tasks i), ii), … are parts (31 parts in total, more than the catalogue estimate of 27). Printed problem points: 8+8+8+12+5+5+8+8+10 = 72; no total is printed, so paper.totalPoints is null. Each problem heading carries an author credit (e.g. “— Oskar Vallhagen.”), kept verbatim in italics at the start of the statement; each solution starts with its printed solution/grading credit, including the printed placeholder “grading schemes by ....”. Problem 7 is titled “A stack of papers” in the problems document and “A pack of papers” in the solutions; the problems-document title is used. The paper mixes theory (1–3, 5–8) and experimental problems (4 Black box, 9 Surface tension), hence roundType mixed. Printed slips kept verbatim: P1 part iv asks for the torque $T$ while the solution calls it $\\tau$; P1 solution “cab be”, “opponents stone”, “components of the acting on arcs”; P4 solution: the headers of both measurement tables are printed as “V (mV) | t (s) | V (mV) | t (s)” and “I (μA) | t (s) | I (12.3 μA) | t (s)” although the first column of each pair holds the time — kept as printed; the second measurement ends “we obtain $\\tau_1 =$ s.” with the value missing (and presumably meaning τ2); option (d) is listed twice; “$R_1 = (I_0/\\mathcal{E} - 1/R_2)-1$” is printed with “−1” on the line instead of an exponent and “$R_2 = (I_f/\\mathcal{E} - R_1 = 6.08$ kΩ” with an unbalanced bracket; P6 solution “to a distance $ym$”; P7 solution: “$v' = \\omega x_0\\sinh(\\ldots)$” (should be cosh) and “$x_0 = -L_0/(2\\sinh(\\omega\\Delta t))$” as printed, the u-small paragraph says “Conversely at very large $v$” and gives accelerations $\\pm u/(g\\mu)$ while the graphs show $\\pm g\\mu$, and the last grading line ends with a stray hyphen “(0.3 pts)-”; P8 solution “$t_1 = \\sqrt{2L/a}$” and a missing full stop before “At that moment”; P9 solution: an unclosed parenthesis in part i, and the final formula for σ uses $h$ where the text uses $t$ for the layer thickness. The official grading lines for P3 iv read “Finding M (0.3 pts)” (text layer shows a subscript artefact). Solution circuit diagrams carry their printed labels “Circuit (A):” … “Circuit (D):” as captions.",
